{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"components/2/text\",\"value_json\":\"\\\"子 is the visible lower component of 学. One source proposes it was added in Western Zhou forms to mark the child as the object of learning; its present-day function remains unresolved.\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"history\",\"value_json\":\"[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"學 is the traditional counterpart of standardized simplified 学. The graphic path from early forms to either modern shape is not established here.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref021\\\",\\\"ref032\\\"]},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A later lexicographic account describes 學 as an abbreviated seal-script form of 斆, which it analyzes as 教 and 冖 with 𦥑 supplying the sound. This received account does not confirm the structure of earlier forms.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref019\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref031\\\"]},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"One source proposes that teaching and learning were represented by the same graph in antiquity, and offers this as an explanation for their historical relation.\\\",\\\"evidence_ids\\\":[\\\"ref127\\\"]}]\"}]}"}}
